Commit:     Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Sun Nov 15 14:36:36 2026 -0500

    iio: adc: qcom-spmi-vadc: expose processed battery voltages
    
    Expose calibrated processed voltages for the existing VBAT_SNS and
    LR_MUX1_BAT_THERM raw channels. Keep their raw reads, names, types and
    prescale ratios, and leave all other channel records unchanged.
    
    For absolute calibration, return a fractional millivolt result with a
    denominator of 1000. This gives new processed interfaces the IIO voltage
    units while allowing processed-scale consumers to retain microvolt
    precision. Preserve existing processed behavior on legacy channels.
    
    Carry Timothy Schmidt's e0e89468dcfc and its preserved 2457eebe0bb6
    prerequisite onto the current IIO maintainer tree. Codex:GPT-6 assisted
    the port and actual-callback/channel-table ASan/UBSan qualification.
    This adds interfaces to raw-only inputs; physical accuracy and the
    combined charging policy remain separate qualification requirements.

